# 8. Auth Model — Ulo (adapted from invitation-only)

Ulo uses:
1) **Standard auth** — Fortify email/password + Sanctum token for members (login screen Stitch a6f02). User stays logged in via SecureStore.
2) **House access token** — crypto-secure, revocable, single-use token for extended family: `POST /house/access` with `token` → backend verifies, grants house scope. Token URLs: `https://app.ulo.house/house/access/<token>` and dev `ulo://house/<token>`. Mobile extracts token, calls backend, backend is authoritative (never decide locally "token valid").
3) **Guest share link** — `https://app.ulo.house/share/rooms/<slug>` public read; no auth required, but contributions gated by `rooms.tier_type`/`doors_open`/`storage_bytes`.

Flow:
```
Invite link tap → App open (cold/warm/background) → extract token/slug → POST verify → SecureStore session → _layout guard → (app) index or (public) welcome
```

No password-less WhatsApp primary — WhatsApp is secondary for invites later if needed.

---

# 9. Session Storage

`expo-secure-store` ONLY for tokens/credentials. Never AsyncStorage / plain file / query param / Zustand / component state.

Startup:
```
App Launch → Restore Session → valid → (app) / no session → (public) welcome / expired → verifying → welcome
```
Never flash welcome while session restore pending.

---

# 10. Backend Contract

Mobile talks to Laravel API only:

```
React Native → HTTPS → Laravel API → PostgreSQL / Stripe|Paystack|PayPal / Storage
```

Backend owns: auth, authorization, house membership isolation, invitation/token validation, rooms, stories, payments + fee calc + verification (webhooks authoritative), storage limits, contribution gates.

Never trust `organization_id` / `house_id` from client. Never calculate fee in client.

---

# 11. API Communication

TanStack Query is mandatory for server state. Do not use `useEffect+useState` fetch.

```ts
const { data, isLoading, error } = useQuery({ queryKey: ['rooms'], queryFn: getRooms });
```

Structure:
```
Screen → Feature Hook (useRooms) → TanStack Query → Feature API (features/rooms/api.ts → apiClient.get('/rooms')) → Shared HTTP Client (src/lib/api/client.ts) → Laravel JSON:API
```

Do not create one giant `src/api.ts`. Domain modules: `features/rooms/{api,queries,mutations,types,components}`, `features/checkout`, `features/house`, `features/payments`, `features/reels`, `features/search`, etc. Wayfinder analogue: `@/actions/` for web — mobile uses `apiClient` with same backend.

Shared HTTP client handles base URL (`EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL`), auth header from SecureStore, serialization, error normalization. No business logic inside client.

---

# 12. Domain Truth — Rooms & Pricing (authoritative)

`config/pricing.php` + `app/Services/RoomService.php` + `routes/web.php` are source of truth — see also `APP.md`/`README.md`.

Rooms: `rooms.room_type = general|wedding|birthday|burial|memorial|anniversary|graduation`
- `general` = free Starter: 1 active room, 50 contributions, 1GB (`tiers.starter`), 30 collection days.
- Every other occasion = Paid Full Room: 10GB (`tiers.full_room`), 12 months access, auto-upgrade via checkout. Paywall redirect if `tier_type !== general` and member tries `/dashboard/rooms/create`.

Pricing: 5 regions, single currency shown, amounts in minor units, savings = 12×monthly − yearly:
- nigeria NGN: Full Room ₦150,000 (15_000_000), Family monthly ₦3,500 yearly ₦35,000 savings ₦7,000
- rest_of_africa USD: $190 / $4.99 / $49.00 save $10.88
- uk GBP: £290 / £7.99 / £79.00 save £16.88
- us_rest_of_world USD: $350 / $9.99 / $99.00 save $20.88
- europe EUR: €350 / €9.99 / €99.00 save €20.88

Family Archive: 25GB (`tiers.family_archive`). Partner referral: 20% commission floor ₦3,000.

Fees: mobile never calculates fees. Backend returns `{ amount, processing_fee, service_fee, total }` — mobile displays only.

---

# 13. Payments — Multi-Gateway polling

Providers: Stripe / Paystack / PayPal per region. Flow:

```
Select occasion/amount → Backend POST /checkout/initialize (idempotent) → return { payment_id, amount, fees, total, provider, reference } → Show breakdown → Confirm → Provider checkout → Backend verifies (webhook+poll) → Poll GET /checkout/{payment}/status every 3s → successful/failed
```

Never show `Payment successful` because checkout sheet closed. Only backend says `successful`. Polling text: `Checking every 3s — do not close` with gold 2px progress bar. Disable double-tap: button `Processing...`, no auto-retry that creates duplicate transactions (idempotency key handled by backend).

History/detail: `GET /payments` paginated + `GET /payments/{payment}` shows purpose, status, reference, dates, total. Use `Intl.NumberFormat` per region currency — centralize in `features/payments/utils/formatCurrency.ts`.

---

# 14. Styling — NativeWind IS TailwindCSS

- `NativeWind` **is** TailwindCSS v4 for RN. Do not add `styled-components`, `tamagui`, etc.
- Prefer `<View className="flex-1 bg-[#000000] px-5">` — no arbitrary inline styles.
- NativeWind does NOT dictate design — Stitch does. Do not make generic Tailwind dashboard.
- Tokens: define centrally `src/constants/theme.ts` + `tailwind.config.js`:
  ```
  primary #C9993A, background #000000, surface #0A0A0A, foreground #F2EDE0, muted #A8A8A8, border rgba(255,255,255,0.08), success/warning/danger semantic
  ```
  Solid colors only. No gradients/glassmorphism/neon/blobs/sparkles/wand/emoji nav.

# 14a. Light Mode — REQUIRED (invert dark tokens, same Stitch design)

The agent MUST ship both **dark (default) + light** modes from day one. Dark is primary (Stitch `Ulo — Black Heritage` pure black) — light is the semantic inversion using **the same token names from §0/§14**, do not invent a new palette.

- Implementation: `src/constants/theme.ts` exports `light` + `dark` objects with identical keys; `tailwind.config.js` uses CSS variables / NativeWind `dark:` not enough — use explicit theme provider (`src/hooks/useTheme.ts` + `ThemeProvider` at `_layout.tsx`) that switches via `Appearance` + persisted preference (`AsyncStorage` for preference, `SecureStore` not needed for theme). Support `light | dark | system` and respect OS `useColorScheme()`. Toggle lives in `Settings & House` (`house/settings.tsx` — Stitch `81c16cd`).
- Stitch mapping: Keep Stitch dark HTML as authored; light is runtime inversion — do NOT regenerate Stitch screens for light. Derive light tokens 1:1 from dark:
  ```
  dark.background  #000000          → light.background  #F2EDE0 (Story Cream) / #FAF6EE
  dark.surface     #0A0A0A/#111111  → light.surface     #FFFFFF
  dark.card        #0A0A0A border rgba(255,255,255,0.08) → light.card #FFFFFF border rgba(0,0,0,0.08) shadow-sm 0 1px 3px rgba(0,0,0,0.06)
  dark.foreground  #F2EDE0          → light.foreground  #0A0A0A (near-black)
  dark.muted       #A8A8A8          → light.muted       #6B6B6B / #8A8A8A
  dark.border      rgba(255,255,255,0.08) → light.border rgba(0,0,0,0.08)
  accent           #C9993A          → same #C9993A in both (gold CTA never changes)
  success/warning/danger keep semantic but ensure contrast on both
  ```
- Tailwind usage: never hardcode `bg-[#000000]` without theme — use `bg-background` / `bg-surface` / `text-foreground` / `border-border` / `bg-primary` that resolve via NativeWind `vars` or `theme[colorScheme].background`. Example:
  ```tsx
  const { colors, scheme } = useTheme();
  <View style={{ backgroundColor: colors.background }} className="flex-1" />
  // or NativeWind: <View className="flex-1 bg-background" />
  ```
  The raw Stitch export `bg-[#000000]` must be converted to theme-aware: `bg-background` (dark #000000 / light #F2EDE0).
- Every screen must be verified in both modes: Dashboard, Room Detail, Wedding Funnel, Pricing, Checkout, Guest Share, Search, Notifications, Analytics, Reels (video stays dark scrim even in light — keep immersive dark), House Access, Client. Take screenshots light+dark for PR.
- Respect `StatusBar` style per scheme (`light-content` on dark, `dark-content` on light) and `SafeAreaView` background = `colors.background`.

---

# 15. Design Philosophy + Anti-Slop

Professional, mature, trustworthy, calm, clear, accessible, human, heritage — appropriate for older family members + financial transactions. Dark premium black feels like private vault.

PROHIBITED by default: gradients, glassmorphism, excessive shadows, neon, blobs, abstract shapes, pill-everything, giant hero, fake stats/testimonials, confetti/sparkles/magic, AI decorations, wand/sparkle/robot emoji. Rounded-2xl only where Stitch shows (32px card max). No `rounded-full` spam.

Cards only when grouping improves hierarchy — avoid `Card>Card>Card`. Prefer spacing/dividers/typography.

---

# 16. Icons / Buttons / Typography

- Icons `lucide-react-native` ONLY — semantic: `Calendar/CreditCard/Users/MessageCircle/Bell/User/Settings/Search/ChevronRight/Check/X/AlertCircle/Clock/Share2/QrCode`. No Sparkles/Wand/Stars/Robot/Magic.
- Buttons: clear label `Make Payment / View Room / Contribute a Story / Confirm Payment`. Icon-only allowed for Back/Close/Search with `accessibilityLabel`.
- Typography: readability first. Hierarchy `Screen title 20px semibold cream / Section 16px / Body 13-14px / Metadata 11-12px`. Minimum tap text 14px for amounts.

---

# 17. Client vs Server State

- Server: TanStack Query (`['rooms'], ['rooms',slug], ['payments'], ['house'], ['search',query], ['notifications']`)
- Persistent sensitive: SecureStore (auth token, house token)
- Client UI: local `useState` (modal, tab, search input) or Zustand for genuine cross-screen shared UI only — never put server data in Zustand.

Invalidate after mutations: payment success → invalidate `['payments'], ['rooms']`.

---

# 18. TypeScript & Folder Structure

Strict TS, no `any` (use `unknown`). Centralize types `features/rooms/types.ts` etc.

```
src/
  app/ (expo-router routes — see §7)
  components/ui/  Button Input Card Avatar Badge Modal BottomSheet EmptyState ErrorState LoadingState
  features/
    auth/{api,queries,mutations,types,session}
    rooms/{api,queries,mutations,types,utils,components/room-card.tsx}
    checkout/{api,queries,types}
    house/{api,queries,types}
    payments/{api,queries,mutations,types,utils}
    reels/{api,queries,types}
    search/{api,queries,types}
    notifications/{api,queries,types}
  lib/api/{client.ts}
  hooks/ stores/ constants/ types/ utils/
```

Feature owns its domain. No `modules/` needless.

---

# 19. Loading / Empty / Error

Every server screen: Loading (skeleton, not blank) / Success / Empty / Error (`We couldn't load your rooms. Try again.` with Retry, never `AxiosError 422`).

Pagination: `FlatList`/`FlashList` + TanStack infinite queries. Never `data.map` inside `ScrollView`.

---

# 20. Security — Secrets, Auth, Org Isolation

- Never hardcode `STRIPE_SECRET`, `PAYSTACK_SECRET`, WhatsApp secrets — backend only. `EXPO_PUBLIC_*` is client-bundled → never secrets.
- Mobile is not security boundary — backend enforces house isolation: user A must not see house B rooms/payments. Frontend hides UX but backend rejects.
- Deep link edge: invalid/expired/revoked/used token, wrong house — show human message, never silently swap account if already authenticated.
- Logout: clear SecureStore + reset TanStack cache + navigate to `(public)/welcome`; never leak previous user's payments/chats.

---

# 21. Deep Links — House/Share

Scheme: `ulo://house/<token>` dev, `https://app.ulo.house/house/<token>` prod universal, `https://app.ulo.house/share/rooms/<slug>` public. Must handle cold/warm/background/after-install (Expo Linking). Extract → `POST /house/access` → backend decides.

Do not add email login/verify/reset unless requested — Ulo is house-token/guest-slug centric.

---

# 22. Quality Gates

Before completing task:

```
npx tsc --noEmit (or project's types:check)
npm run lint
npx expo-doctor
php artisan test --compact --filter=related (backend contract)
vendor/bin/pint --dirty --format agent (if PHP touched)
```

Tests priority: auth, token verification, payment status/polling, house isolation, query invalidation, deep links.

Never ship fake data (`John Doe ₦1M`).

